<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 489)</h2>
<p><b>Exports show progress, and Save on quit actually quits.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: choosing Save when quitting cancelled the quit.</b> The check that asked "is it saved now?" was reading state the save had already replaced, so it always answered no. For a session with no file yet it was worse — the save panel opened without blocking, so the answer came back before you had chosen anything. Save now saves and quits; Cancel still cancels.</li>
<li><b>New: exports report progress in the header</b> — a whole-session reel names itself and its shot count and fills as it goes. It is the longest thing Asobi does and it ran with nothing on screen to say so.</li>
<li>Playing a movie stand-in forward no longer rebuilds its decoder every tenth of a second. It reads forward in one pass instead, which removes a lot of repeated seeking.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
